WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.601 --> 00:00:03.184
(upbeat music)

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:07.680
- Recently, Apple announced
these MacBook Pros

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:09.440
with some bold claims.

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:12.660
- [Woman] Gets up to 21
hours of video playback

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:14.730
which is 10 additional hours.

00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:18.020
And the longest battery
life ever on a Mac notebook.

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:19.880
- Are you sure about that Apple?

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:22.000
Come on, someone had to test it.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.540
So I set up this 16 inch MacBook Pro

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:26.500
which has an M1 Max chip

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:29.930
to play this video clip for 21 hours.

00:00:29.930 --> 00:00:31.420
- [Woman] And the 16 inch model

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:34.490
gets up to 21 hours of video playback.

00:00:34.490 --> 00:00:36.740
- [Joanna] And I did
exactly what Apple said,

00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:40.150
wifi off, and brightness at
eight clicks from the bottom,

00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:43.233
and I unplugged for a long time.

00:00:45.156 --> 00:00:47.739
(upbeat music)

00:00:50.745 --> 00:00:52.550
- [Woman] Gets up to 21.

00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:54.910
- [Joanna] Okay, not quite 21 hours,

00:00:54.910 --> 00:00:57.160
but wow, that's long enough to last you

00:00:57.160 --> 00:01:01.240
a 15 hour flight from New York
to Shanghai, and then some.

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:03.220
Although, if you were planning to use wifi

00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:04.720
and chat and surf the web,

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:07.000
then you'd be looking at
more an eight hour flight

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:08.670
from New York to Munich.

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:10.150
So why did I do all this?

00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:14.410
Well, because the promise of a
truly all day laptop is here,

00:01:14.410 --> 00:01:16.880
and you don't even need
bigger batteries to do it all.

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:18.790
The real savings comes from Apple's shift

00:01:18.790 --> 00:01:23.510
from Intel chips to its own
M1 Pro and M1 max chips.

00:01:23.510 --> 00:01:25.090
So when Apple said.

00:01:25.090 --> 00:01:28.740
- And the longest battery
life ever on a Mac notebook.

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:30.513
- There was only one thing to do.

00:01:31.970 --> 00:01:32.880
Testing.

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:34.580
These are crooked aren't they?

00:01:34.580 --> 00:01:36.550
Okay, before I get into
those test results,

00:01:36.550 --> 00:01:38.210
let's talk about these,

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:40.610
which have the dream laptop design.

00:01:40.610 --> 00:01:43.780
At least in comparison
to the old MacBook Pros.

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:45.930
There is a full SD size SD card slot,

00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:47.650
and an HDMI port.

00:01:47.650 --> 00:01:51.500
Sure, the SD card still
sticks out, but I'll take it.

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:55.053
There's a row of real
function keys, RIP touch bar.

00:01:56.240 --> 00:01:58.980
And yes, the Magsafe charger is back.

00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:01.810
You can still charge via
these USB-C ports too.

00:02:01.810 --> 00:02:04.360
The XCR screens are bright and beautiful,

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:05.580
and the size of the screens

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:08.510
are really the main thing
that separates these two.

00:02:08.510 --> 00:02:09.850
Oh, and price.

00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:14.850
The 14 inch starts at
$2,000, and the 16 at $2500.

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:16.750
Really pricey.

00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:20.410
I could live without this
notch around the webcam though.

00:02:20.410 --> 00:02:22.480
To make the bezzles
around the screen smaller,

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:26.080
they had to fit the 1080P
webcam in someplace.

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:27.660
Don't get me wrong, camera quality

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:30.140
is way better than the previous laptops,

00:02:30.140 --> 00:02:31.890
but still no iPhone selfie camera.

00:02:31.890 --> 00:02:34.270
The bigger leaps though
are inside these machines,

00:02:34.270 --> 00:02:37.910
with Apple's own M1 Pro and M1 Max chips.

00:02:37.910 --> 00:02:39.910
The chips are incredibly fast,

00:02:39.910 --> 00:02:41.820
I couldn't get these laptops to slow down

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:44.670
even when multi-tasking
things like video editing,

00:02:44.670 --> 00:02:46.030
gaming, and more.

00:02:46.030 --> 00:02:47.520
And when I asked Apple's Tom Boger

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:49.050
what the biggest improvement in going

00:02:49.050 --> 00:02:51.407
from Intel to Apple was, he said.

00:02:51.407 --> 00:02:53.607
- [Tom] "I Sum it up in a very simple term

00:02:53.607 --> 00:02:55.637
"of performance per watt.

00:02:55.637 --> 00:02:57.490
"it's game changing."

00:02:57.490 --> 00:02:59.330
- [Joanna] What does that even mean?

00:02:59.330 --> 00:03:01.720
Allow me to explain with this stuff.

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:04.820
Let's say this container
of Powerade is well, power,

00:03:04.820 --> 00:03:06.010
or watts.

00:03:06.010 --> 00:03:08.170
And well, I need performance.

00:03:08.170 --> 00:03:09.003
Cheers.

00:03:09.003 --> 00:03:10.300
Sipping the watts for power,

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:12.470
and then using the power to do things.

00:03:12.470 --> 00:03:13.533
Powered up.

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:18.370
Intel chips based on X86 architecture

00:03:18.370 --> 00:03:21.907
have good performance, but
are more power thirsty.

00:03:21.907 --> 00:03:24.200
So to do this high performance,

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:26.280
I've gotta chug more power.

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:27.670
Intel processor.

00:03:27.670 --> 00:03:30.050
Apple's chips based on
our arm architecture

00:03:30.050 --> 00:03:33.210
have good performance too,
but are more power efficient.

00:03:33.210 --> 00:03:36.540
So to do this high
performance, I need less power

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:38.900
and I can just sip the watts.

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:40.240
Like a fine wine.

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:42.580
So you get it, using its own chips

00:03:42.580 --> 00:03:45.250
Apple gets more performance per watt,

00:03:45.250 --> 00:03:47.910
or in other words, it can
have the same battery size

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:49.910
as a computer with an Intel chip,

00:03:49.910 --> 00:03:52.740
but that battery can
theoretically last longer.

00:03:52.740 --> 00:03:55.966
Okay, back to computers,
and these actual tests.

00:03:55.966 --> 00:03:58.670
The old Intel 16 inch MacBook Pro,

00:03:58.670 --> 00:04:01.330
and the new Apple chip 16 inch MacBook Pro

00:04:01.330 --> 00:04:04.220
both have the same 100 watt hour battery.

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:05.230
Take a look at this chart

00:04:05.230 --> 00:04:07.130
on my video battery test though.

00:04:07.130 --> 00:04:08.600
The machines with Apple chips

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:10.390
last at least five hours longer

00:04:10.390 --> 00:04:14.450
on both streaming and
local video playback tests.

00:04:14.450 --> 00:04:16.770
About that 21 hours of battery life,

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:18.420
Apple's fine print says it got there

00:04:18.420 --> 00:04:20.640
using a 16 inch test machine

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:22.800
with an M1 Pro processor,

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:26.050
a step down from the M1 Max in my unit.

00:04:26.050 --> 00:04:28.500
Plus there's more that's
not even in that fine print,

00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:30.530
like turning off the keyboard backlight,

00:04:30.530 --> 00:04:32.090
and the true tone display.

00:04:32.090 --> 00:04:33.890
And the company said
that the white background

00:04:33.890 --> 00:04:36.843
in my video sample may
have drained extra juice.

00:04:38.690 --> 00:04:40.660
When I got an identical MacBook Pro

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:42.180
with the M1 Pro chip,

00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:43.670
adjusted all the settings,

00:04:43.670 --> 00:04:46.040
and used Apple's recommended test videos,

00:04:46.040 --> 00:04:49.980
just $60 plus on iTunes, guess what,

00:04:49.980 --> 00:04:52.850
21.5 hours.

00:04:52.850 --> 00:04:54.900
But here's the thing, video rundown tests

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:57.180
never tell the whole battery story,

00:04:57.180 --> 00:05:00.060
it's just not that intensive
of a processing task.

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:03.270
It's more like stretching
than jumping jacks.

00:05:03.270 --> 00:05:05.460
Plus we all use our laptops differently.

00:05:05.460 --> 00:05:06.870
So I kept track of the battery life

00:05:06.870 --> 00:05:10.360
when I used Safari, Slack, and
played music in Apple Music.

00:05:10.360 --> 00:05:12.630
The 16 inch ran for eight hours,

00:05:12.630 --> 00:05:15.170
the 14 inch for six and a half hours.

00:05:15.170 --> 00:05:16.670
That was at least three hours longer

00:05:16.670 --> 00:05:18.800
than Apple's Intel machines.

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:20.370
When I did that test with Chrome,

00:05:20.370 --> 00:05:22.250
things dropped by an hour or so.

00:05:22.250 --> 00:05:24.880
Nope, not the promised double digit hours.

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:27.480
Although when I got out this bad boy,

00:05:27.480 --> 00:05:29.690
a 290 watt battery,

00:05:29.690 --> 00:05:31.900
I was able to finally hit those.

00:05:31.900 --> 00:05:34.190
And yes, I realize it's
basically just like

00:05:34.190 --> 00:05:35.650
being plugged into the wall.

00:05:35.650 --> 00:05:37.970
The 13 inch MacBook Pro with the M1 chip

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:39.050
announced last year

00:05:39.050 --> 00:05:40.520
actually lasted just as long

00:05:40.520 --> 00:05:42.513
as those laptops in my daily use.

00:05:43.940 --> 00:05:46.350
So I'll throw that back at you Apple.

00:05:46.350 --> 00:05:47.600
When you say.

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:51.210
- And the longest battery
life ever on a Mac notebook.

00:05:51.210 --> 00:05:52.600
- If you've got wifi off,

00:05:52.600 --> 00:05:55.700
and brightness at 50%,
and videos downloaded.

00:05:55.700 --> 00:05:58.170
But please do not confuse
this with complaining.

00:05:58.170 --> 00:06:00.210
After years of slimming down laptops

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:02.040
and cramming in small batteries,

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:04.400
Apple's got a great strategy here.

00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:07.399
Power efficient chips and big batteries,

00:06:07.399 --> 00:06:10.970
I just wish the fine
print was large print.

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:14.013
- And the longest battery life ever.

00:06:14.013 --> 00:06:16.193
- This is how I'm gonna be
for all Apple events now.

